# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.egg
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- Environment / secrets ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Data ----
# Raw and derived data are downloaded and rebuilt, never committed. The whole
# corpus is ~38 competition files from football-data.co.uk, re-fetchable in
# minutes by `make data`, and it changes every match week — committing it would
# be both large and permanently stale.
#
# Nothing under data/ is committed, and no sample slice is either. The
# provider publishes no licence granting redistribution, so this repository
# ships none of its data — see the note in README. The unit suite needs none:
# it runs against synthetic fixtures shaped like the real files, so CI passes
# on a clean checkout with no network. Tests that need real data are marked
# `integration` and skip when it is absent.
data/raw/*
data/processed/*
data/features/*
data/reports/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep
!data/features/.gitkeep
!data/reports/.gitkeep

# ---- Models ----
models/*
!models/.gitkeep

# ---- MLflow ----
# Experiment tracking state is a local artefact store, not source. The runs
# worth keeping are promoted to the model registry and their metrics written
# into docs/, which is what gets reviewed.
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# ---- Tooling ----
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- Editors / OS ----
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Stray lockfiles from other package managers. This project pins with
# requirements*.txt; a second, unmaintained lockfile in the tree is a source of
# confusion, not of truth.
uv.lock
poetry.lock
